# Ownership after a `+` attachment

This table is normative. It applies PART 0 S1 to S5 and PART 9 §17 L3 (CARVE-P0-024, CARVE-P9-067) to the line that follows a block a continuation marker attached, and names the clause or ruling that decides each owner (carve#5658). `tests/plus-ownership-table.test.mjs` walks every cell against the spec model.

An attached fence owns every line up to its end. Only the fence's own end condition (its closer, or the first blank for a marker-line `+`) ends it; a line that misses the host ends only an own-line attachment.

## Axes

- Host: list item `- `, footnote body `[^a]: `, definition body `: ` under `:: t`, block quote `> `.
- `+` form: marker-line (`- +`), own-line (`- p` / `+`), stacked (the host opens on an outer item's marker line, `- - +`, so its marker column is 2).
- Attached source, written at the host's marker column: unclosed code fence, closed code fence, paragraph, table, attribute-shaped run (`{#i` / ` .y}`), refused-brace-shaped run (`{.x` / `.y}`, CARVE-P2-035). In the span context the last two source shapes are code-span text, not block-position runs.
- Follower probe for item, note and description: content column, marker column, column 0, refused marker-column `+` then a content line, or a fence one column right of the marker then a content line. The Owner cell names the final content line of a two-line probe; the marker or fence opener is read by S1 and S3 at its own column.
- Follower probe for a quote: deep content (`>   zq`), quote content (`> zq`), marker column (`zq`), off-column `+` (`> +`) then content, or a fence one column past quote content then content. The `>` prefix changes source columns, so these names do not reuse the list-host columns. A blank without `>` ends the quote (PART 0 S2).
- Context: plain, or the block's paragraph holds an open inline code span (a backtick run with no closer).

## Owners

- Block: the attached block keeps the line. For a fence it is payload; for a paragraph or a refused run it continues that paragraph; for an attribute run it is the block that takes the attributes.
- Host: the host's body keeps the line as a new block.
- Parent: the host is closed and the line is read in the container that holds the host: the outer item for a stacked host, the document otherwise.
- Document: every frame is closed.
- Span: the line is code text in the open inline code span; the owner is the Block.

## Cells

The first row that matches a cell decides it. `any` matches every value on that axis.

|= Id  |= Host          |= Form                |= Block                      |= Follower                                   |= Blank |= Context |= Owner                                          |= Decided by                                                                          |
